WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Two cars collide at a junction.

2
00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.540
Two witnesses see exactly the same thing.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.560
Later, an officer asks the first: how fast
were the cars going when they hit each

4
00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.390
other?

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.490
The second witness hears one word changed:

6
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.980
when they smashed into each other?

7
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.060
A week later, both are
asked what they remember.

8
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.290
Why might their memories now differ?

9
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:24.090
Did one have a worse view?

10
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.890
Is one exaggerating?

11
00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.770
In this mission, you'll find out
what makes a leading question:

12
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.010
one that suggests the answer,
like asking did you see the knife,

13
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.790
instead of a knife.

14
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:40.880
And you'll discover how a false memory
can feel just as real as a true one.

15
00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: explain why the
two witnesses' memories differ.
